# Testing (Java / Spring Boot)

## TDD

- Red/Green/Refactor; write failing test first; no implementation without tests (escape: trivial/config).

## Stack

- JUnit 5, AssertJ, Mockito; spring-boot-starter-test; spring-boot-webmvc-test for MockMvc; spring-security-test for security context; WireMock for HTTP stubs; ArchUnit for architecture tests.

## Unit Tests

- **Naming:** *Test.java; describe class/method; should {expected} when {condition}.
- **Structure:** @ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class); @Mock dependencies; @InjectMocks subject; given/when/then or Arrange/Act/Assert.
- **MockMvc:** MockMvc with or without full context; perform get/post; andExpect(status().isOk()), jsonPath; andDo(print()) for debug.

## Integration Tests

- @SpringBootTest (or slice); @AutoConfigureMockMvc; WireMock for external APIs; Testcontainers for DB if needed.
- Use @Sql or flyway/liquibase for test data; rollback or separate DB.

## Conventions

- Test behavior and contracts; avoid testing implementation; use WireMock for external calls; clear test data; deterministic tests.

## Anti-Patterns

- Real external calls in unit tests; no cleanup; flaky tests; testing private methods; missing security context in secured tests

